module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveBorelPairStructure
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.RationalHighestWeightData
import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Geometrically.Reduced
import Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.AlgebraRepresentation.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic

/-! # Restricted simple modules tensored with Frobenius pullbacks

Source: Jantzen (2003), II.3.16--3.17 (not locally available); Milne, Algebraic
Groups (2017), 22.54--22.55, pp.481--482, and 23.25, pp.492--493.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-restricted-frobenius-tensor-simplicity)

The pullback uses the actual global-sections map of f. The diagonal coaction is
constructed by the existing coefficient-multiplication map. Simplicity and highest
lines use the shared coaction predicates, including scheme-theoretic invariance.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
universe u v w
open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped TensorProduct MonObj
namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RationalHighestWeight

/-- Diagonal coaction on V tensor the pullback of W along f. On finite tensor
presentations cV(v) = sum vi tensor ai and cW(w) = sum wj tensor bj, its value is
sum (vi tensor wj) tensor (ai * f-sharp(bj)). The vector space W is unchanged.
Source: Milne, Sections 4a--4e and 22.55.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-restricted-frobenius-tensor-simplicity) -/
def tensorPullbackCoaction
    {F : Type u} [Field F] {S : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))} [IsAffine S.X.left]
    {V : Type v} [AddCommGroup V] [Module F V]
    {W : Type w} [AddCommGroup W] [Module F W]
    (f : S ⟶ S)
    (cV : V →ₗ[F] V ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra S)
    (cW : W →ₗ[F] W ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra S) :
    V ⊗[F] W →ₗ[F] (V ⊗[F] W) ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra S :=
  HopfAction.tensorCoefficients F (coordinateAlgebra S) F V W ∘ₗ
    TensorProduct.map cV ((coordinateMap f).toLinearMap.lTensor W ∘ₗ cW)

/-- Steinberg simplicity with an arbitrary isogeny inducing multiplication by p
on the character lattice, and preserving the chosen torus and unipotent radical.
Source: Jantzen, II.3.16--3.17; Milne, 22.54--22.55 and 23.25.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-restricted-frobenius-tensor-simplicity)

Proof plan:
The constructed map is counital and coassociative: pullback along a group
homomorphism preserves the coordinate counit and comultiplication; multiplying
Hopf coefficients gives the tensor coaction laws from the two given laws.
1. By lem-sfb-scalar-p-isogeny-relative-frobenius, write f = h after relative
   Frobenius, with h an isomorphism. Semisimplicity implies reductivity by
   lem-sfb-reductive-borel-pair-structure. Smoothness gives reduced coordinates
   by sbc-lem-smooth-geometrically-reduced. Taking pth roots in F writes every
   element of the twisted coordinate algebra as b tensor 1; its Frobenius image
   is b^p. Reducedness implies injectivity, so f-sharp is injective. On dual-number
   points Frobenius kills the tangent part, hence df = 0.
2. By lem-sfb-restricted-module-infinitesimal-simplicity, V is infinitesimally
   simple. Let A be the unital F-subalgebra of End_F(V) generated by its tangent
   action. Its submodules are exactly the subspaces stable under that action.
   Scalar Schur (lem-sfb-simple-algebra-scalar-endomorphisms) identifies End_A(V)
   with F. A finite F-basis generates over End_A(V), so
   lem-sfb-finite-simple-double-centralizer gives A = End_F(V).
3. For an S-stable subspace N of the tensor product, evaluate at e + epsilon x.
   Since df = 0, comparison of epsilon coefficients makes N stable under
   d-rho(x) tensor 1, hence under every a tensor 1 for a in End_F(V).
   Choose a basis v1,...,vd and set Z = {w : v1 tensor w lies in N}.
   Matrix units E_1i show every coefficient of an element of N lies in Z;
   E_j1 show every vj tensor Z lies in N. Thus N = V tensor Z.
4. After any scalar extension, stability under rhoV(s) tensor rhoW(f(s)) and
   rhoV(s) inverse tensor 1 implies stability under 1 tensor rhoW(f(s)).
   The first coordinate functional gives stability of Z under f-pullback of W.
   Evaluate at the universal S-point. For pi : W to W/Z, the obstruction
   (pi tensor 1)cW(z) is killed by 1 tensor f-sharp. This map is injective,
   by expansion in a basis of W/Z, so Z is stable in W itself. Simplicity of W
   gives Z = 0 or W. Therefore N = 0 or the whole tensor product. Nonzero basis
   vectors in V and W give a nonzero pure tensor, completing simplicity.
The same argument includes p = 2, zero highest weights, products and S = 1. -/
theorem restricted_frobenius_tensor_simplicity
    {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F]
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP F p]
    (S T B U : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F))))
    [IsAffine S.X.left] [IsAffine T.X.left] [IsAffine U.X.left]
    (hS : IsSemisimpleGroupScheme S.X)
    (hsc : ∀ (S' : Over (Spec (.of F))) [GrpObj S'],
      IsSemisimpleGroupScheme S' → ∀ (g : S' ⟶ S.X) [IsMonHom g],
      Surjective g.left → IsFinite (GrpObj.ker g).hom →
      (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
        (x : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ GrpObj.ker g)
        (s : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ S'),
        (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι g) * s = s * (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι g)) → IsIso g)
    (iT : T ⟶ S) (iB : B ⟶ S) (j : T ⟶ B) (iU : U ⟶ B)
    (hT : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT)
    (hsplit : ∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r))
    (hB : IsBorelGroupScheme iB.hom.hom) (hj : j ≫ iB = iT)
    (hUclosed : IsClosedSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom)
    (hUnormal : IsNormalSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom)
    (hUsmooth : Smooth U.X.hom) (hUconnected : ConnectedSpace U.X.left)
    (hUunipotent : SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent U)
    (hUmax : ∀ (N : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iN : N ⟶ B),
      IsClosedSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom → IsNormalSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom →
      Smooth N.X.hom → ConnectedSpace N.X.left →
      SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent N → ∃ g : N ⟶ U, g ≫ iU = iN)
    [IsCommMonObj T.X] [IsCommMonObj (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)]
    (aS : ModObj T.X S.X) (aB : ModObj T.X B.X)
    (Φ : Finset (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))))
    (P : RootDatum Φ
      (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)))
    (b : P.Base) [P.IsReduced]
    (hconjS : aS.smul = (iT.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 S.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj S.X)
    (hconjB : aB.smul = (j.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 B.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj B.X)
    (hroot : ∀ α : Φ, P.root α = α.val)
    (hpair : ∀ (χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (ν : Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)),
      ν.toMul.hom.hom ≫ χ.toMul.hom.hom =
        (𝟙 (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)) ^ (P.toLinearMap χ ν))
    (hweights : ∀ χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)),
      χ ∈ Φ ↔ χ ≠ 0 ∧ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T S aS χ.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    (hpositive : ∀ α : Φ,
      b.IsPos α ↔ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T B aB α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    (f : S ⟶ S) (hfsurj : Surjective f.hom.hom.left)
    (hfker : IsFinite (GrpObj.ker f.hom.hom).hom)
    (fT : T ⟶ T) (hfT : fT ≫ iT = iT ≫ f)
    (fU : U ⟶ U) (hfU : fU ≫ iU ≫ iB = iU ≫ iB ≫ f)
    (hfchar : ∀ χ : T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F),
      fT ≫ χ = χ ^ p)
    {V : Type v} [AddCommGroup V] [Module F V] [FiniteDimensional F V]
    {W : Type w} [AddCommGroup W] [Module F W] [FiniteDimensional F W]
    (cV : V →ₗ[F] V ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra S)
    (cW : W →ₗ[F] W ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra S)
    (hcoassocV : HopfAction.Coassociative F (coordinateAlgebra S) V cV)
    (hcounitV : HopfAction.Counital F (coordinateAlgebra S) V cV)
    (hcoassocW : HopfAction.Coassociative F (coordinateAlgebra S) W cW)
    (hcounitW : HopfAction.Counital F (coordinateAlgebra S) W cW)
    (hsimpleV : IsSimple cV) (hsimpleW : IsSimple cW)
    (lam mu : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
    (hhighestV : HasHighestWeight cV iT (iU ≫ iB) lam.toMul)
    (hhighestW : HasHighestWeight cW iT (iU ≫ iB) mu.toMul)
    (hdomV : ∀ α ∈ b.support, 0 ≤ P.toLinearMap lam (P.coroot α))
    (hdomW : ∀ α ∈ b.support, 0 ≤ P.toLinearMap mu (P.coroot α))
    (hrestricted : ∀ α ∈ b.support, P.toLinearMap lam (P.coroot α) < (p : ℤ)) :
    HopfAction.Coassociative F (coordinateAlgebra S) (V ⊗[F] W)
        (tensorPullbackCoaction f cV cW) ∧
      HopfAction.Counital F (coordinateAlgebra S) (V ⊗[F] W)
        (tensorPullbackCoaction f cV cW) ∧
      IsSimple (tensorPullbackCoaction f cV cW) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.RationalHighestWeight
